Text detection and recognition models for `ocrs`
================================================

`text-detection.rten` and `text-recognition.rten` in this directory are the English
models of the `ocrs` project, by Robert Knight, distributed unmodified.

    Source:   https://github.com/robertknight/ocrs-models
    Weights:  https://ocrs-models.s3-accelerate.amazonaws.com/text-detection.rten
              https://ocrs-models.s3-accelerate.amazonaws.com/text-recognition.rten
    Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
              (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The models were trained on the HierText dataset (Long et al., 2022), which is itself
distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0; the licence of the training data is why the weights
carry it.

CC BY-SA 4.0 asks for attribution and for the same licence on adaptations of the
licensed material. The files above are shipped byte for byte as they were published:
they are not adapted, and the application that reads them is a separate work that
merely uses their output. This notice, kept beside the files inside the application
bundle, is the attribution.

The `ocrs` source code itself is a separate matter: the crate is under MIT OR
Apache-2.0 and is covered by the third-party notices of the application.
